      "message": "They are in the same file: `redfishPcieGenerationFromDbus()` at pcie_util.hpp:139 and `redfishPcieDeviceTypeFromDbus()` at :174 both start their nullopt branch with `.empty()` ||, and `dbusSlotTypeToRf()` is the only one of the three without it. On why it would be empty, PDI types SlotType as an enum defaulting to Unknown so a conforming producer never sends an empty string, but bmcweb reads it as a plain std::string and cannot tell an unset value from a bad one, and today that costs the whole GET a 500; I have expanded the commit message to say this.",
